Paper side of the second-round exploratory analyses: macros, five tables and the account figure; class-split macros for Llama and gpt-oss; generator wording (field class, no stage names, registered claim level); decisions row

ex_review_paper reads the three new stages (Ex macros for the account by writer and class, the
baselines and the horizon transfer, the missed-item accuracies, the zero system after the shift and the
classes of the cited key's misses; tab_writers, tab_baselines, tab_misses, tab_zero_after, tab_json_arm,
fig_account). The top-level keys of the new stage analyses start with explore_. The class-split datasets
cover Llama and gpt-oss. The structured-field class is "field" in every generated table, "stage 2" is gone
from the generated tables, and the registered claim level reads "registered claim: two-factor account with
quantitative prediction". Tests: the wording guard over paper/generated and the Llama and gpt-oss datasets.

